WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.782 --> 00:00:03.365
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.110
- [Narrator] In the French
Riviera lies a medieval town

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.250
that's held one industry at its very heart

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.920
for the last 300 years.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.680
This is Grasse; this is the
world's capital of perfume.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.693
This is the city of scents.

00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:27.735
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:30.485
(romantic music)

00:00:39.965 --> 00:00:42.630
- Some of the big names that
come from here like Chanel,

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.970
Chanel No. 5, Dior, of
course, and Louis Vuitton.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.200
It's something that's understood here.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.340
It's a community; it's a language;

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.263
it's something that people share.

00:02:37.713 --> 00:02:39.660
- My name is Jessica Buchanan,

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.403
and I am an independent perfumer.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.250
I came to Grasse for perfumery school.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.660
So what I do is, in very simple contexts,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.120
mixing together raw materials
for various different uses,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.030
whether it's a perfume that
one would wear to, for example,

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.623
a candle.

00:02:57.623 --> 00:03:01.899
I think to create a good
perfume, I like to allow

00:03:01.899 --> 00:03:04.676
six months to a year.

00:03:04.676 --> 00:03:07.150
This is a very creative process.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.397
When I sit in front of the
perfumer's organ and create,

00:03:10.397 --> 00:03:15.263
it's like sitting in front of
a piano and composing music.

00:03:15.263 --> 00:03:18.479
Yeah, I think there's
something in the air here.

00:03:18.479 --> 00:03:21.646
(upbeat piano music)

